## Plan

_Written by `claude-3` (claude, `opus`, strong) ([run](https://github.com/Jlore-Studios/JackiOh/actions/runs/40740132858)) before anyone built this. The night bot's builder starts from this section: edit it here to change the plan._

## Goal

The viewer's own hand cards can wear **hand hints**: a quiet row of small pips in the face's top-left corner, under the cost gem. Each pip has an icon, an optional number, a dimmed state and an accessible label through `t()`. The hints come from one list, `HAND_HINTS` in `apps/web/src/game/handHints.ts`. Each entry is `{ id, icon, applies(card, view) }` and reads only the `CardView` and `PlayerView`. `HandHints.tsx` draws them in the list's order. The row takes no pointer event, draws nothing when no hint applies, and appears only in `Hand.tsx`'s `yours` branch: never on the opponent's backs, the R434 revealed hand, the board, the deck builder or the collection. The shipped list is empty, so players see no change. Tests use a hint defined in the test file.

## Files to touch

| Path | new/change | What |
|---|---|---|
| `apps/web/src/game/handHints.ts` | new | types `HintShown`, `HandHint`; `HAND_HINTS = []`; `hintsFor()` |
| `apps/web/src/game/HandHints.tsx` | new | `handHintsTestid()`, default component `HandHints` |
| `apps/web/src/game/handHints.css` | new | `.hand-hints`, `.hand-hint`, `.hand-hint > img`, `.hand-hint-n`, dimmed state, fx-copy rule |
| `apps/web/src/game/Card.tsx` | change | new prop `hintRow?: ReactNode`, rendered as a child of the face root; header line |
| `apps/web/src/game/Hand.tsx` | change | props `view?`, `hints?`; passes `<HandHints>` as `hintRow` in the yours branch; header paragraph |
| `apps/web/src/game/Board.tsx` | change | `view={view}` on the `side="you"` `<Hand>` only |
| `apps/web/README.md` | change | one **Hand hints** paragraph |
| `apps/web/src/game/HandHints.test.tsx` | new | every test below |

Do not touch: `cards/CardFace.tsx`, `cards/icons.tsx` (no icon is added: the list ships empty), `cards/inspect/*`, `i18n/zh-CN.json`, `board.css`, anything outside `apps/web` but its README, `spec/`, `.github/`, `.harness/`, `bot/`, `scripts/`, any `package.json` or lockfile. No ruling is needed: this is presentation only. What governs it: SPEC §10.8 and CLAUDE.md rule 7 (the hints read the view only), R434 (the revealed hand gets no hints), and R711000 (`i18n.test.ts`).

## Steps

1. **Create `apps/web/src/game/handHints.ts`.** Give it a `//` header: "#2267: the hand hints, one list in drawing order. A hint reads the card's `CardView` and the `PlayerView` and nothing else (CLAUDE.md rule 7, SPEC §10.8). Adding a hint is one entry here plus its icon in `cards/icons.tsx`. The list ships empty." Then:
   ```ts
   import type { CardView, PlayerView } from "@jackioh/shared";
   import type { IconName } from "../cards/index.ts";

   export type HintShown = {
     /** One short number the pip prints, when the hint has one. */
     n?: number;
     /** Lower opacity and no colour (handHints.css). */
     dimmed?: boolean;
     /** The pip's name for a screen reader, already through `t()`: the hint calls `t()` itself, at render, never at module scope. */
     label: string;
   };

   export type HandHint = {
     /** Unique in the list: the pip's `data-hint` and React key. */
     id: string;
     icon: IconName;
     /** Null when the hint does not apply to this card. */
     applies: (card: CardView, view: PlayerView) => HintShown | null;
   };

   /** The shipped hints, in drawing order. */
   export const HAND_HINTS: readonly HandHint[] = [];

   /** The hints that apply to `card`, in the list's order, each with what it shows. */
   export function hintsFor(card: CardView, view: PlayerView, hints: readonly HandHint[] = HAND_HINTS): { hint: HandHint; shown: HintShown }[] {
     return hints.flatMap((hint) => {
       const shown = hint.applies(card, view);
       return shown === null ? [] : [{ hint, shown }];
     });
   }
   ```

2. **Create `apps/web/src/game/handHints.css`.** Open it with a `/* */` header that says:
   - The row sits top-left, under the cost gem and above the name ribbon. The fan lays each card over the right part of the one before (board.css `.hand-slot + .hand-slot`), and the phone's peek shows only the top half of a card, so the top-left stays in sight.
   - Sizes are in em of the hand card's own font-size (board.css `.card`, `.hand-you .card-hand`).
   - The look is quiet: the theme's tokens, a thin line and a soft backing, no glow, no motion.
   - The row takes no pointer event.
   - The cosmetics are on `.cf`, and the row sits outside `.cf`.

   Use only palette and theme tokens. No colour literal and no `font-size` without a `--type-*` step (`palette.test.ts`, `typescale.test.ts`). No selector may contain `.cf` or `.cf-` (`typography.test.ts`). The rules:
   ```css
   .hand-hints {
     position: absolute;
     z-index: 4;
     top: 19%;
     left: 4%;
     display: flex;
     flex-wrap: nowrap;
